---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import evidence from '../../../public/data/pmd/evidence.json';
const base = evidence.arms[0].nll;
const relativeGain = (base - evidence.arms[1].nll) / base * 100;
const repo = `${evidence.source.repository}/tree/${evidence.source.revision}`;
---
<BaseLayout title="PMD · Does personalization know whose preferences?" description="Explore frozen preference-modeling results: identity controls, differences across users, and history size. 94 known users; no live model or new experiments.">
<div class="pmd container-content py-14">
  <nav class="crumb"><a href="/demo/">Research artifacts</a><span>/</span><span>PMD</span></nav>
  <header class="intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Preference Modeling Diagnostics · Frozen results explorer</p>
    <h1>Does personalization know<br class="wide-only" /> <em>whose</em> preferences?</h1>
    <p class="lede">A small predictive gain is more convincing when it disappears under the wrong identity. Explore what happened in a bounded, CPU-only study.</p>
    <div class="meta"><span>94 known users</span><span>Unseen prompts</span><span>Equal-user weighting</span></div>
    <div class="hero-stats"><div><strong>{relativeGain.toFixed(3)}<small>%</small></strong><span>relative reduction in NLL</span></div><div><strong>67<small> / 94</small></strong><span>users with lower test NLL</span></div><p>This is a small held-out predictive effect—not an accuracy gain of 0.879 percentage points, a new personalization algorithm, or a deployment claim.</p></div>
  </header>
  <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Explorer sections"><a href="#identity">01 / Identity</a><a href="#users">02 / Users</a><a href="#history">03 / History</a><a href="#evidence">Sources ↗</a></nav>

  <section id="identity" class="lab-section">
    <div class="section-heading"><span class="number">01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">The negative controls</p><h2>Change the identity. Does the gain remain?</h2></div></div>
    <p>The representation and shared model stay frozen. Correct-user adaptation uses the person's training history; controls break the link between identity and history.</p>
    <fieldset class="segmented"><legend>Choose how to display the same frozen results</legend><label><input type="radio" name="metric" value="delta" checked /> Change from pooled</label><label><input type="radio" name="metric" value="nll" /> Absolute NLL</label></fieldset>
    <p id="metric-explanation" class="chart-note">ΔNLL = arm − pooled baseline. Negative is better. Values are not percentages.</p>
    <div class="control-chart" id="control-chart" role="img" aria-label="Change in NLL: pooled 0; correct user minus 0.011780; wrong user plus 0.000972; shuffled ID plus 0.000583."><div class="axis-labels"><span>Lower NLL / better ←</span><span>→ Higher NLL / worse</span></div>
      {evidence.arms.map((arm, i) => <div class:list={['arm', arm.id]}><div class="arm-label"><strong>{arm.label}</strong><small>{i === 0 ? 'No individual adaptation' : i === 1 ? 'Each user’s own history' : `${arm.repetitions} control repetitions · mean`}</small></div><div class="track"><span class="baseline-line"></span><span class="arm-dot" data-arm={arm.id} style={`left:${((arm.nll-base+0.014)/0.016)*100}%`}></span></div><output data-value={arm.id}>{i === 0 ? '0.000000' : `${arm.nll-base>0?'+':''}${(arm.nll-base).toFixed(6)}`}</output></div>)}
      <div class="axis-labels ticks"><span data-axis="min">−0.014</span><span data-axis="max">+0.002</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>A useful check, with a modest result.</strong><p>Correct-user adaptation reduced NLL; both control means were slightly worse than pooled. This supports identity-linked predictive information under this design. It does not establish what psychological traits the model learned, or guarantee that every control repetition loses the gain.</p></div>
    <details><summary>Inspect exact values and control definitions</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Day 2B · Equal-user test NLL, lower is better</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Condition</th><th scope="col">NLL</th><th scope="col">Δ from pooled</th></tr></thead><tbody>{evidence.arms.map(arm=><tr><th scope="row">{arm.label}</th><td>{arm.nll.toFixed(6)}</td><td>{(arm.nll-base).toFixed(6)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Wrong-user: deranged assignments of fitted user adaptations (500 repetitions). Shuffled ID: history identities shuffled while preserving history counts, followed by refitting (100 repetitions). These are different controls, not independent user samples.</p></details>
  </section>

  <section id="users" class="lab-section">
    <div class="section-heading"><span class="number">02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Look past the average</p><h2>Better on average does not mean better for everyone.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="user-summary"><div class="user-stack" role="img" aria-label="67 of 94 users improved, 27 worsened, zero tied"><span class="improved">67 improved</span><span class="worsened">27 worsened</span></div><p>Mean ΔNLL <strong>−0.011780</strong> · Median <strong>−0.010998</strong></p><p class="chart-note">Paired user-bootstrap 95% interval for mean ΔNLL: [−0.017497, −0.006157]. Each user has equal weight; the median user has only three test contexts.</p></div>
    <details class="distribution"><summary>Open the original per-user effect figure</summary><figure><a href="/images/pmd/user-effects.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/images/pmd/user-effects.png" alt="Original frozen PMD figure showing the distribution of per-user held-out NLL changes." loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>Original figure, copied byte-for-byte from the frozen artifact. Open for full resolution. Per-user numerical rows are not publicly committed, so this page does not reconstruct individual records from the image.</figcaption></figure></details>
  </section>

  <section id="history" class="lab-section">
    <div class="section-heading"><span class="number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Exploratory · Day 2C</p><h2>How much history is enough?</h2></div></div>
    <p>More history brought a gradual average NLL gain. Which preferences were observed also mattered. These results reuse the observed test set and are exploratory, not a new confirmatory test.</p>
    <div class="history-layout"><div><label for="history-size" class="field-label">Observed distinct training prompts</label><select id="history-size">{evidence.history.map((row,i)=><option value={i} selected={i===2}>{row.history_level==='ALL_AVAILABLE' ? 'All available (median 12 per user)' : row.history_level==='0' ? '0 · Pooled baseline' : `${row.history_level} preferences`}</option>)}</select><div class="history-readout" aria-live="polite"><strong id="history-gain">23.0%</strong><span>of the all-history NLL gain</span><p>Absolute ΔNLL: <b id="history-delta">−0.002713</b></p><p>Mean within-user SD across history subsets: <b id="history-sd">0.009405</b></p><p id="history-repeat-note" class="chart-note">50 deterministic nested history subsets per user.</p></div></div><div class="curve"><svg viewBox="0 0 600 290" role="img" aria-label="Exploratory curve: 1 preference captures 7.7 percent of the all-history gain, 3 captures 23.0, 5 captures 35.4, 8 captures 56.4, and 10 captures 70.0."><line x1="54" y1="224" x2="565" y2="224" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".3"/><line x1="54" y1="40" x2="565" y2="40" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".15" stroke-dasharray="4 5"/><text x="54" y="28">Share of all-history NLL gain</text><text x="10" y="46">100%</text><text x="23" y="229">0%</text><polyline points={evidence.history.slice(0,6).map((r,i)=>`${65+i*96},${224-r.gain_fraction_of_all_available*184}`).join(' ')} fill="none" stroke="#3155d9" stroke-width="3"/>{evidence.history.slice(0,6).map((r,i)=><g><circle data-history-point={i} cx={65+i*96} cy={224-r.gain_fraction_of_all_available*184} r={i===2?7:4} fill="#3155d9"/><text x={65+i*96} y="248" text-anchor="middle">{r.history_level}</text></g>)}<text x="300" y="278" text-anchor="middle">Observed preferences per user</text></svg><p class="chart-note">The dashed line is the separate all-available-history reference. Equal spacing represents the tested history levels, not a continuous numerical x-axis. Point summaries only; no uncertainty bands are shown.</p></div></div>
    <details><summary>Inspect the full history table</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Frozen exploratory summaries · 94 users at every level</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">History</th><th scope="col">ΔNLL</th><th scope="col">Share of all-history gain</th></tr></thead><tbody>{evidence.history.map(r=><tr><th scope="row">{r.history_level}</th><td>{r.delta_nll.toFixed(6)}</td><td>{(r.gain_fraction_of_all_available*100).toFixed(1)}%</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
  </section>
  <section id="evidence" class="lab-section evidence"><p class="eyebrow">Read the evidence</p><h2>Frozen results, open sources.</h2><p>No model runs in this page. Controls and history levels change the displayed recorded results, not a live model. Source revision <code>{evidence.source.revision.slice(0,12)}</code>.</p><div class="source-links"><a href={repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Frozen repository ↗</a><a href={`${repo}/docs/PMD_TECHNICAL_NOTE.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Technical note ↗</a><a href="/data/pmd/evidence.json" download>Results + source hashes ↓</a><a href="/data/pmd/history-curve.csv" download>Full history CSV ↓</a></div><p><strong>Scope:</strong> 94 known users with sufficient training history, prompt-disjoint evaluation, fixed linear representation, and a bounded wave-1 subset of Community Alignment v1.1. Anonymous identity may proxy topic exposure, session, or interface effects. No causal mechanism, unseen-user generalization, or population-wide benefit is established.</p><p class="chart-note">Data attribution: Zhang et al., <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.09650">Community Alignment Dataset</a>, CC BY 4.0. Dataset-derived results were filtered and transformed by Baixin Guo. Original code and documentation: MIT. This explorer presents existing analyses; it does not extend the frozen experiment.</p></section>
</div>
<script>
import data from '../../../public/data/pmd/evidence.json';
const base = data.arms[0].nll;
function setMetric(metric: string) {
 const delta = metric === 'delta';
 const lo = delta ? -.014 : 1.325;
 const hi = delta ? .002 : 1.344;
 data.arms.forEach(arm => {
  const v = delta ? arm.nll-base : arm.nll;
  const dot = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-arm="${arm.id}"]`);
  if(dot) dot.style.left = `${(v-lo)/(hi-lo)*100}%`;
  const out = document.querySelector(`[data-value="${arm.id}"]`);
  if(out) out.textContent = `${delta && v>0?'+':''}${v.toFixed(6)}`;
 });
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.baseline-line').forEach(line=>line.style.left=`${((delta?0:base)-lo)/(hi-lo)*100}%`);
 document.querySelector('[data-axis="min"]')!.textContent=lo.toFixed(3);
 document.querySelector('[data-axis="max"]')!.textContent=hi.toFixed(3);
 document.getElementById('metric-explanation')!.textContent=delta?'ΔNLL = arm − pooled baseline. Negative is better. Values are not percentages.':'Equal-user negative log-likelihood (NLL). Lower is better. Zoomed axis; the vertical line marks pooled NLL, not zero.';
 document.getElementById('control-chart')!.setAttribute('aria-label', data.arms.map(a=>`${a.label}: ${(delta?a.nll-base:a.nll).toFixed(6)}`).join('; '));
}
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="metric"]').forEach(input=>input.addEventListener('change',()=>setMetric(input.value)));
const select = document.getElementById('history-size') as HTMLSelectElement;
function setHistory(){
 const idx=Number(select.value), row=data.history[idx];
 document.getElementById('history-gain')!.textContent=`${(100*row.gain_fraction_of_all_available).toFixed(1)}%`;
 document.getElementById('history-delta')!.textContent=row.delta_nll.toFixed(6);
 document.getElementById('history-sd')!.textContent=idx===0||idx===6?'Not applicable (one fit per user)':row.mean_within_user_sd_delta_nll.toFixed(6);
 document.getElementById('history-repeat-note')!.textContent=idx===0?'Pooled baseline: no individual history used.':idx===6?'One fit per user using all available training history. Median history: 12 distinct prompts.':'50 deterministic nested history subsets per user. SD describes history-subset variability, not a confidence interval.';
 document.querySelectorAll<SVGCircleElement>('[data-history-point]').forEach(dot=>{dot.setAttribute('r',Number(dot.dataset.historyPoint)===idx?'8':'4');dot.style.opacity=idx===6?'.5':'1';});
}
select.addEventListener('change',setHistory);
setMetric('delta'); setHistory();
</script>
<style>
.pmd{max-width:1080px;color:var(--color-ink)}.crumb,.eyebrow,.meta,.section-nav,.number,.chart-note,figcaption{font-family:var(--font-mono)}.crumb{display:flex;gap:.7rem;font-size:.72rem;margin-bottom:2.5rem;color:var(--color-text-muted)}.eyebrow{text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.65rem;letter-spacing:.09em;color:var(--color-primary);line-height:1.7}.intro h1{font-size:clamp(2.3rem,5vw,4.2rem);line-height:1.08;margin:1rem 0}.intro em{color:var(--color-primary)}.lede{max-width:680px;font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text-dim)}.meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem;font-size:.65rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.meta span{border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:30px;padding:.35rem .75rem}.hero-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1.6fr;gap:1.7rem;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:1.8rem;border-radius:12px;margin:2rem 0}.hero-stats strong{display:block;font-size:2.6rem;line-height:1.2;font-family:var(--font-display);color:var(--color-primary)}.hero-stats small{font-size:1.1rem}.hero-stats span{font-size:.75rem}.hero-stats p{font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0;color:var(--color-text-dim)}.section-nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1.2rem;font-size:.7rem;padding:1rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule)}.section-nav a{color:var(--color-brand)}.lab-section{padding:3.2rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-light);scroll-margin-top:90px}.section-heading{display:flex;gap:1.2rem;align-items:flex-start}.number{font-size:.8rem;padding-top:.4rem;color:var(--color-text-muted)}h2{font-size:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2rem);line-height:1.3;margin:.3rem 0 1rem}.lab-section>p,.takeaway p,.evidence p{line-height:1.8;color:var(--color-text-dim)}.segmented{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.8rem;border:0;margin:1.5rem 0 .7rem;padding:0}.segmented legend{font-size:.75rem;margin-bottom:.7rem}.segmented label{display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;padding:.6rem .85rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:8px;font-size:.8rem;cursor:pointer}.segmented label:has(input:checked){background:var(--color-brand-subtle);border-color:var(--color-primary)}input{accent-color:var(--color-primary)}.chart-note,figcaption{font-size:.67rem;line-height:1.8;color:var(--color-text-muted)}.control-chart{margin:1.3rem 0;padding:1.4rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:10px;background:var(--color-surface)}.axis-labels{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;font-size:.65rem;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-bottom:.8rem}.arm{display:grid;grid-template-columns:190px minmax(0,1fr) 100px;gap:1rem;align-items:center;min-height:70px}.arm-label strong{display:block;font-size:.8rem}.arm-label small{display:block;font-size:.65rem;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-top:.3rem}.track{height:30px;position:relative;background:var(--color-page-warm);border-radius:3px}.baseline-line{position:absolute;left:87.5%;height:100%;border-left:1px dashed var(--color-text-muted)}.arm-dot{position:absolute;top:9px;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--color-text-muted);transform:translateX(-50%)}.correct .arm-dot{background:#3155d9}.wrong .arm-dot{background:#c64d3e}.shuffled .arm-dot{background:#93622a}.arm output{font:500 .8rem var(--font-mono);text-align:right}.ticks{margin:1rem 116px 0 206px}.takeaway{border-left:3px solid var(--color-primary);padding:1rem 1.3rem;background:var(--color-brand-subtle);margin:1.5rem 0}.takeaway p{font-size:.88rem;margin:.5rem 0 0}details{margin-top:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem}summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600}details p{font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.8;margin-top:1rem;color:var(--color-text-dim)}.table-scroll{max-width:100%;overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.78rem;margin-top:1rem;text-align:left}caption{text-align:left;padding:.6rem 0;color:var(--color-text-muted)}th,td{padding:.8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-light)}td{font-family:var(--font-mono)}.user-stack{display:flex;margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;min-height:54px}.user-stack span{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:.6rem;font-size:.85rem}.improved{width:71.2766%;background:#3155d9;color:white}.worsened{width:28.7234%;background:#f2d7d2;color:#70382e}.user-summary p{line-height:1.8;font-size:.85rem}.distribution img{width:100%;height:auto;margin:1.5rem 0 .7rem}.history-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.7fr;gap:2rem;margin-top:1.5rem;padding:1.5rem;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:10px}.field-label{display:block;font-size:.75rem;margin-bottom:.7rem}select{width:100%;max-width:100%;background:var(--color-page);border:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:.8rem;border-radius:6px;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--color-ink)}.history-readout{padding-top:1.5rem}.history-readout>strong{display:block;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:3rem;color:var(--color-primary);line-height:1.2}.history-readout>span{font-size:.75rem}.history-readout p{font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.8;margin-top:1rem}.curve svg{width:100%;height:auto;color:var(--color-text-dim)}.curve text{font:12px var(--font-sans);fill:currentColor}.source-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.8rem 1.3rem;font-size:.8rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.source-links a{color:var(--color-brand);border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule)}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #3155d9;outline-offset:4px}.evidence code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.evidence{border-bottom:0}
@media(max-width:700px){.hero-stats{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;padding:1.2rem;gap:1.2rem}.hero-stats p{grid-column:1/-1}.history-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:1rem}.arm{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 90px;gap:.4rem;margin:1rem 0}.arm-label{grid-column:1/-1}.arm-label small{display:inline}.track{height:28px}.ticks{margin-left:0;margin-right:96px}.control-chart{padding:1rem}.wide-only{display:none}.section-heading{gap:.7rem}.lab-section{padding:2.3rem 0}.user-stack span{font-size:.7rem}.source-links{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}.segmented label{font-size:.75rem}.axis-labels{font-size:.6rem}}
</style>
